@bs-humany/muscle-data

This package is in the Data tier of ADR-009 and is distributed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (see LICENSE). The package as a whole carries that
licence, its schema and validation code included, because the data and the code that holds it
share the same source files.

The muscle definitions are laid on this project's skeleton, and part of what they hold is
measured on it: each attachment names a site that @bs-humany/skeleton locates on the bone meshes
of @bs-humany/assets-anatomical, the muscle length ranges in src/ranges.ts are swept on those
bones, the fibre lengths of the neck muscles are fractions of the distance between their
attachments there, and the intercostals are sized on the rib lengths in the rib arcs of
assets-anatomical. Those values are derivatives of the following, and carry its licence:

  "BodyParts3D - The Database Center for Life Science - CC-BY-SA 2.1 Japan"
  "Z-Anatomy - The libre 3D atlas of anatomy - CC-BY-SA 4.0"

Z-Anatomy authors: Kousaku Okubo (original BodyParts3D model), Gauthier Kervyn (design, 3D,
anatomy), Marcin Zielinski (Blender add-on), Lluis Vinent (Unity development).
Source: https://github.com/LluisV/Z-Anatomy (Resources/Models/FBX/SkeletalSystem100.fbx) and
https://github.com/Z-Anatomy/Models-of-human-anatomy.

The other values come from sources whose licences permit their use in a CC BY-SA work. Each value
carries its citation at the point of use, and docs/sources/bibliography.md is the complete list:

  - MyoSuite myo_sim (MyoHub), Apache-2.0, cited caggiano2022: the peak isometric forces, optimal
    fibre lengths and tendon slack lengths that the tools/cli/bin/generate-*-muscles.mjs
    generators extract, and the source-model travel in src/sourceTravel.ts, measured by running
    those models. The licence and the pinned commit are in tools/validate-external/myo_sim.
  - Seth et al. (2019), CC BY, cited seth2019: the shoulder girdle parameters.
  - Gray's Anatomy (1918), public domain, cited gray1918: which bony feature each muscle attaches
    to.
  - The published measurements and sizing rules that the neck and thorax sets apply (zheng2013,
    vasavada1998, bruno2015), used as facts with a citation, not copied as a work.

The other bs-humany code packages, which load this data, remain Apache-2.0: they are not
derivatives of it. See ADR-009 and ADR-011, and the root NOTICE.
